<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Faisal ibn Turki Al Saud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1865</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Faisal ibn Turki <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of the Second Saudi State, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> in two reigns, 1834–1838 and 1843–1865. Between them an Egyptian expedition took him captive to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, but he escaped and regained power. He backed his ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-ibn-rashid">Abdullah ibn Rashid</a> in taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hail">Ha'il</a> in 1836, founding the Rashidi Emirate of Jabal Shammar, and his long second reign consolidated the emirate.</p></div>
